WEBVTT

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.730
Tell me, Freecell!

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:11.540
Did I really...

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:14.500
Was it my fault your mom died?

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.340
I just don't get it.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.510
What did I do?

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:21.430
What happened?

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:24.290
I wanna know the truth!

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.910
You're brutal, Kaito.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:31.230
You try to remember, but you can't.

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:34.290
I want to forget, but I can't.

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:37.260
And yet you want me to tell you?

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:40.380
You have an obligation to

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:42.490
remember the truth on your own.

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:44.770
Isn't that right, Kaito?

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:48.610
I look forward to our game.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:57.990
Dammit!

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:23.850
Lost

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.980
Tesaguri de sagashiteta
I've searched, groping

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:30.900
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
The answer to a future that's been closed off

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:32.780
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
Is nowhere to be found

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:36.150
Hashiru shoudou, ima kaidoku funou
The impulse to run, it's impossible to decipher now

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:37.860
Found

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:42.080
Kudaketa hazu no unmei o
A fate that was supposedly smashed

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:46.580
Mijuku na yume no naka de kikoeta kitanda
I've come to hear it within that half-formed dream:

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:49.380
Saigo made I'll be there for you
Until the end, I'll be there for you

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:52.500
Tachidomaranai, kono hari dake wa
It won't stop, not this needle

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.840
Boku no asu o kizamu oto o tsukisasu
It will pierce the sound that engraves my tomorrow

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:57.720
Shinjitsu kara nigetara ima
If I run from the truth, then now...

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.430
Genjitsu ni mo maketara ima
If I lose to reality, then now...

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:01.800
Nani ga nokoru no?
What will remain?

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:04.010
(Nokoru no?)
(Will remain?)

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:06.390
Kazoekirenai kono kizu dake ga
These countless wounds of mine

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:09.850
Boku no kinou o zanzou to shite kataru
They tell of my yesterday as an afterimage

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:11.560
Unmei ga hodoketemo ima
Even if fate were unraveled, now...

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:13.400
Sonzai o kowashitemo ima
Even if my existence were smashed, now...

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:16.240
Boku no michi o yuku yo
I will travel my path

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:18.400
It's now or never

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:19.490
That is what they say

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:21.570
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:25.240
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:26.410
That is what they say

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:28.580
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:32.080
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.290
That is what they say

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:35.710
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:41.930
The Truth Behind the Smile

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:48.280
There's no way Kaito can
do puzzles right now.

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:53.380
True, thanks to Ana, we've
pulled up from rock bottom.

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:56.380
But we're a long way from
a definitive solution.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:02.590
I, Ana, think Kaito can't see
the truth in the darkness,

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:04.390
so he can't move.

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:05.280
Yeah...

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:10.470
Why did I even come along?

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:12.960
I can't do anything.

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:15.320
Not yet, huh?

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:17.300
No word from Upperclassman Jikukawa.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:20.690
If we can prove my supposition,

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:23.240
we may be able to save Kaito.

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:35.920
Even using all the POG's systems,

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:38.910
it takes so long to
analyze all this data.

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:41.860
No need for me to get involved, is there?

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:44.350
Mr. Principal!

00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:45.500
When did you...

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:47.560
You think for yourself,

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.920
choose the appropriate
action based on the situation...

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:51.910
You've grown.

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:55.460
Gammon and Cubik as well.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:59.350
In other words, the
situation we face is...

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:00.500
quite severe.

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:08.790
Change the format of the game?

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:11.180
Yes.

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:13.330
The remaining two battles,

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:16.660
in other words, Doubt vs. Gammon

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:19.940
and Freecell vs. Kaito, will be a single game,

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:22.490
a two-on-two, tag-team battle.

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:24.400
Tag-team battle?

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.870
What's the meaning of this, Whi?

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:30.040
It's "Whist," Miss Mela.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:33.690
ME-LAN-CHO-LY!

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:36.450
My apologies for the wait.

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:39.460
How wonderful!

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:42.000
I can't accept this.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.530
Changing the format of our sacred battle

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:47.240
just before the fact...

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:49.090
For what reason?

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:50.300
Where's the harm?

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:51.700
I don't care.

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:53.670
I can play with Kaito.

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:55.730
That doesn't change.

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:56.810
Freecell!

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:58.600
My apologies.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:03.940
Klondike is apparently most
pleased with this change.

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:06.530
Klondike is?!

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.320
Then it can't be helped.

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:09.950
Rather...

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:15.510
If it is Klondike's
wish, then by all means.

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:26.800
What?

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:28.470
You did?

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:29.960
That's right.

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:31.900
It was me who made the

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:34.840
request for the last game
to be a tag-team battle.

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:36.740
Why would you do that?

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:40.320
Me and Kaito, we can
get two wins at once.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:43.320
Do that and we're 3-2, and we win.

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:45.760
Got a problem with that, Kaito?

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:54.830
Kaito, where are you going?

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:56.730
To wash my face.

00:05:57.310 --> 00:05:58.210
If we're gonna do this...

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:00.390
We will win!

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:04.280
Kaito...

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:06.940
This will be tough in his state.

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:09.020
That's why I went for a tag-team battle.

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:12.460
I'll give him as much follow-up as I can.

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:15.110
If he's still gonna get beat...

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:18.350
I'm writin' Kaito off.

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:22.110
Gammon!

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:24.100
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:25.800
This is for me.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:28.120
When that idiot is his usual self,

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:31.620
that's when my genius
really shines through.

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:35.230
I'll do it too! For Kaito!

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:37.020
I, Ana, will cheer him!

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:38.490
Me too!

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:40.610
Ana, let's cheer him on together.

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:41.580
Sounds good!

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:44.310
Hey! Cheer me on too!

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:45.210
I'll try.

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:50.130
Do everything you possibly can, dammit.

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:52.550
Like your life depends on it!

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:18.760
Very well, the last Rink Slider game
shall now commence.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:23.370
Kaito, Freecell, Gammon

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:25.530
and Doubt shall proceed in that order.

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:27.070
Choose your slider and move as you like,

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:29.450
backward and forward, left and right.

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:32.960
You will stop when you
encounter a hindrance.

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:36.660
If you cannot move, you
will pass on your turn.

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:41.410
When one of your team reaches
the center goal, you win.

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:43.770
By winning, you will receive two points,

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:46.440
at the same time determining the overall winner.

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:51.490
Note that we have implemented
some special rules.

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:55.150
If you stop at any of
the rink's four panels,

00:07:55.150 --> 00:07:59.250
when the sliders moves, a
"dust hole" will appear.

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:03.380
It will not disappear until
the player in question moves.

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:08.760
With this format, team play is the key.

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:10.590
You have to read the movements

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:13.130
of your partner
as well as your opponent.

00:08:13.640 --> 00:08:16.470
Can Kaito do that right now?

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:22.640
Now then, the last game...

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:23.920
Play.

00:08:24.610 --> 00:08:26.470
Kaito, good luck!

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:27.720
Kaito!

00:08:27.720 --> 00:08:28.680
Let's go!

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:33.810
Here I come, Kaito.

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:36.200
Let's play up.

00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:40.610
Whoa, there.

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:17.200
Dumbass, keep your wits about ya!

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:22.540
When they move those sliders,

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:26.370
holes open up that limit
their movement options.

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:28.600
This is a difficult puzzle.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:36.410
I'm happy, Kaito...

00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:39.090
To be able to play with you like this.

00:09:41.070 --> 00:09:43.850
I've waited so long for you.

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:45.850
For so long...

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:48.730
I'm sure she's happy:

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:50.480
my mama up in Heaven.

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:57.050
What was that feeling just now?

00:09:57.050 --> 00:09:58.360
Kaito!

00:09:58.770 --> 00:10:00.960
Concentrate on the puzzle!

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:02.870
Quit thinkin' about other crap!

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:04.750
Pitiful.

00:10:13.490 --> 00:10:16.230
I thought this would turn
into a long battle, but...

00:10:16.230 --> 00:10:18.050
Not a bad battle, is it?

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:21.300
With one exception, that is.

00:10:27.010 --> 00:10:28.190
Kaito...

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:30.100
He doesn't have the same edge as always.

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:32.360
Their team play is being restricted.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:35.290
Gammon is trying to give him support,

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:37.610
but at some point they'll
close in on him.

00:10:38.210 --> 00:10:40.990
When that happens, we lose.

00:10:42.150 --> 00:10:44.000
If only I'd receive word...

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:48.620
Still nothing, Upperclassman Jikukawa?

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:53.790
This way!

00:11:06.490 --> 00:11:08.020
I...

00:11:08.020 --> 00:11:11.860
I really made his mom...

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:13.190
That's right.

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:17.040
You made her die.

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:20.820
Wounded and sad, she finally died.

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:24.690
Because you broke your promise to me.

00:11:24.690 --> 00:11:26.930
I..I don't get it.

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:30.790
Why would breaking my
promise make your mom...

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:42.070
My kind, pretty mama...

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:44.490
My treasure...

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:47.550
You stole my mama from me.

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:50.350
That is all the truth!

00:11:58.950 --> 00:11:59.940
Rook!

00:12:14.610 --> 00:12:16.450
Why? Why?

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:19.010
Why does Freecell...

00:12:19.010 --> 00:12:20.710
have the same eyes as Rook?

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:22.460
No!

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:24.470
I hate that.

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:25.510
It makes me shudder.

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:28.530
That laugh...

00:12:29.440 --> 00:12:30.920
He's laughing!

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:32.210
Why?

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:34.880
Kaito's the enemy, right?

00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:36.900
So, how can he laugh?

00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:43.010
You are weak of heart, Kaito Daimon.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:46.120
You're not an opponent worthy
of the Orpehus Order.

00:12:46.650 --> 00:12:48.620
Don't let 'em trick ya, Kaito!

00:12:50.510 --> 00:12:53.000
Kaito, it's your turn.

00:12:54.930 --> 00:12:56.750
But you can't move, can you?

00:12:56.970 --> 00:12:58.500
Well, you pass.

00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:07.200
It's not good.

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:09.980
Kaito can't concentrate
on the puzzle anymore.

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:11.420
Kaito!

00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:12.860
That's right.

00:13:12.860 --> 00:13:16.770
It's because you broke your promise
that my mama died.

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:19.520
I'll have you honor your promise.

00:13:20.220 --> 00:13:21.650
I don't get it.

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:23.610
Promise?

00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:25.280
What promise?

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:27.780
Continue battling me through puzzles.

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:32.290
As long as you live,
you cannot refuse me!

00:13:33.300 --> 00:13:35.450
Wh..What the heck?

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:36.790
Why do you and I have to...

00:13:37.310 --> 00:13:41.550
Because you broke your
promise and killed my mama!

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:47.210
Kaito...

00:13:47.990 --> 00:13:51.510
What's this "promise" he
keeps going on about?!

00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:54.660
What the hell?

00:13:54.660 --> 00:13:57.560
Just what's he doing to Kaito?

00:13:57.960 --> 00:13:59.010
Come on!

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:01.060
They still haven't analyzed the data?

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:08.520
There it is!

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:15.080
This...

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:23.510
No, Kaito, that will-

00:14:23.510 --> 00:14:25.480
Giving advice is against the rules.

00:14:34.920 --> 00:14:35.970
I...

00:14:36.910 --> 00:14:38.230
I won't lose!

00:14:52.550 --> 00:14:54.540
It's here, from Upperclassman Jikukawa!

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:56.750
Ah, Cube!

00:15:03.810 --> 00:15:06.890
As I thought, my supposition was right!

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:13.780
Now's our chance!

00:15:14.460 --> 00:15:16.420
The next time Kaito moves,

00:15:16.420 --> 00:15:18.430
it will be three turns to the goal!

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:21.980
But can Kaito even see that right now?

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:27.780
I won't let you.

00:15:28.210 --> 00:15:29.540
This is bad.

00:15:29.540 --> 00:15:32.370
If Kaito doesn't block Freecell's route,

00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:34.560
Freecell's sure to win!

00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:37.040
Kaito!

00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:39.100
Hey, Daimoron!

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:41.260
Pull it together, Kaito!

00:15:41.260 --> 00:15:43.920
What's the matter, Kaito?

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:45.800
This is boring.

00:15:46.410 --> 00:15:49.310
Play with me more.

00:15:49.310 --> 00:15:50.170
More!

00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:03.010
What's wrong with him?

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:08.860
That boy loves his mama.

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:13.710
But I'm sure he cares for Kaito too.

00:16:13.710 --> 00:16:15.180
No way!

00:16:15.180 --> 00:16:16.960
Then how can he laugh?

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:19.610
How can he laugh as
he makes Kaito suffer?

00:16:21.970 --> 00:16:24.750
That smile isn't real.

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:26.300
Exactly!

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:28.700
Cube!

00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:30.510
His spirit's been broken.

00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:32.380
Broken?

00:16:32.910 --> 00:16:35.510
Kaito, the analysis is complete!

00:16:35.900 --> 00:16:39.140
They're being swallowed
up by the Orpheus Rings!

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:47.360
During Cubik's game,

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:49.470
he secretly recorded the Orpheus Order's

00:16:49.470 --> 00:16:52.390
brainwaves and mental activity.

00:16:52.390 --> 00:16:54.450
When that was analyzed by the POG's

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:55.820
computers, we found...

00:16:56.390 --> 00:16:59.260
Their Orpheus Rings are normally active,

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:02.660
and they are being swallowed up
by that immense power.

00:17:03.390 --> 00:17:04.210
Yes.

00:17:04.800 --> 00:17:07.830
There's no way they can stay rational
in that condition!

00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:10.090
Both their thoughts and feelings

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:12.330
are bound to be incredibly twisted!

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:15.840
There's no truth to these
"facts" Freecell speaks of!

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:18.600
You can't believe him, Kaito!

00:17:21.650 --> 00:17:23.430
Such pitiful words of deception.

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:26.850
We are Phi-Brain Children.

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:29.190
We are one with the Orpheus Rings,

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:32.080
and we control them!

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:35.470
That's what Rook once thought too!

00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:36.240
But...

00:17:37.770 --> 00:17:40.370
With his ambitions and sense
of friendship twisted,

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:42.330
he turned against Kaito!

00:17:44.570 --> 00:17:48.140
Those are the eyes of someone
swallowed up by the Orpheus Ring.

00:17:49.150 --> 00:17:50.150
Kaito!

00:17:51.180 --> 00:17:53.510
Remember your promise!

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:56.690
You said, "I'll solve
all puzzles," right?!

00:17:57.320 --> 00:17:59.470
That's your promise to us!

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:01.970
Keep it!

00:18:11.280 --> 00:18:12.440
The duel...

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:13.860
begins now.

00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:15.360
Freecell...

00:18:15.590 --> 00:18:16.490
Kaito!

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:17.740
Kaito!

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:19.990
Kaito...

00:18:20.270 --> 00:18:23.570
Jeez, took you frggin' long enough!

00:18:23.570 --> 00:18:25.020
Let's go, Gammon!

00:18:28.090 --> 00:18:30.240
Well, it's your turn.

00:18:34.390 --> 00:18:36.300
I pass, Kaito.

00:18:38.530 --> 00:18:39.880
Good!

00:18:41.960 --> 00:18:44.300
Now comes the true battle.

00:18:55.840 --> 00:18:59.030
Kaito and Gammon are incredible!

00:18:59.310 --> 00:19:01.450
They're working in perfect sync!

00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:05.790
Damn, I can't pursue!

00:19:06.230 --> 00:19:08.620
Doubt has been shut out from the puzzle!

00:19:16.160 --> 00:19:18.600
This is the end!

00:19:28.440 --> 00:19:30.770
Yes, they've secured the goal!

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:35.540
Winners: Mr. Gammon and Mr. Kaito.

00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:38.220
Their combined record is
three wins, two losses.

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:41.530
Victory goes to the Root
Gakuen Academy team.

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:44.470
We did it!

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:45.760
He won.

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:47.540
Kaito won!

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:51.040
You guys really helped me out.

00:19:51.990 --> 00:19:53.770
Then, take us out for dinner.

00:19:53.770 --> 00:19:55.210
A heapin' helping of food!

00:19:55.210 --> 00:19:57.210
You better eat it all!

00:19:58.640 --> 00:19:59.820
Nonoha...

00:20:00.390 --> 00:20:02.970
I kept my promise.

00:20:03.910 --> 00:20:05.220
Yeah!

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:09.730
Impossible, I actually lost?!

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:12.580
It can't be, it just can't be!

00:20:12.580 --> 00:20:16.260
That is Kaito Daimon's true power?

00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:17.780
Fr..Freecell...

00:20:18.740 --> 00:20:20.030
Beautiful...

00:20:21.140 --> 00:20:23.160
Such beautiful play.

00:20:23.160 --> 00:20:24.910
You're incredible, Kaito.

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:28.820
Kaito, let's...

00:20:28.820 --> 00:20:31.850
Let's begin puzzle time, together.

00:20:32.590 --> 00:20:33.290
Hurry up.

00:20:33.950 --> 00:20:35.310
More...

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:37.540
Come on, hurry!

00:20:38.580 --> 00:20:43.800
Kaito Daimon, you are the one
that broke Freecell's spirit.

00:20:44.230 --> 00:20:45.860
Come on, Kaito!

00:20:45.860 --> 00:20:47.550
Let's do more puzzles!

00:20:51.050 --> 00:20:53.810
Very well, Root Gauken team,
if you would please leave.

00:21:02.560 --> 00:21:05.780
Even if he was swallowed
up by the Orpheus Ring,

00:21:05.780 --> 00:21:08.580
Freecell was telling the truth.

00:21:09.060 --> 00:21:12.460
I killed his mom.

00:21:12.960 --> 00:21:14.750
I, Ana, think...

00:21:15.490 --> 00:21:19.680
If that were true, you
would be a bad person.

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:21.760
You'd have to make up for it.

00:21:22.370 --> 00:21:23.490
Ana...

00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:25.920
Fight and shine your light,

00:21:25.920 --> 00:21:28.230
on the truth within the darkness.

00:21:28.230 --> 00:21:31.720
Use that light to warm that
person's heart, Kaito.

00:21:33.440 --> 00:21:38.360
Well, these folks don't seem
the type to go off quietly.

00:21:38.520 --> 00:21:39.780
BAM!

00:21:39.780 --> 00:21:41.860
We'll beat 'em back down anytime.

00:21:41.860 --> 00:21:43.110
Right, Kaito?

00:21:43.250 --> 00:21:45.740
Yeah, I'll do it.

00:21:46.800 --> 00:21:49.990
Who's really at fault?

00:21:53.270 --> 00:21:54.330
Freecell?

00:21:54.750 --> 00:21:57.030
I will go all-out on a puzzle with you.

00:21:57.460 --> 00:21:59.500
That day is sure to come.

00:22:05.490 --> 00:22:09.930
This incident let us acquire
a multitude of intriguing data.

00:22:10.260 --> 00:22:13.510
Especially the tag-team
battle of the last game.

00:22:14.980 --> 00:22:18.590
Shall we deal with Freecell and
the other losing members?

00:22:19.940 --> 00:22:21.230
Not necessary.

00:22:23.380 --> 00:22:25.930
They still have their uses.

00:24:02.290 --> 00:24:03.580
Hey, you all!

00:24:03.580 --> 00:24:05.630
This is no time to be
lying around the place.

00:24:05.630 --> 00:24:08.210
Erena said she'd take us
all to her beach house!

00:24:08.210 --> 00:24:10.560
Yahoo! Let's go to the southern islands!

00:24:10.560 --> 00:24:13.200
That's right! Think of the southern islands,
think of celebs!

00:24:13.200 --> 00:24:14.920
Think of celebs, think of swimsuits!

00:24:15.530 --> 00:24:18.010
I will show you everything I've got!

00:24:18.010 --> 00:24:20.980
Next time, "Puzzle Time Won't Begin!"

00:24:20.000 --> 00:24:26.670
Puzzle Time Won't Begin!

00:24:21.420 --> 00:24:22.850
Sorry for the wait, everyone!

00:24:22.850 --> 00:24:24.270
Tropical time...

00:24:24.270 --> 00:24:25.410
Let's begin!
